1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,218
Two products advertise semantic AI search.

2
00:00:04,381 --> 00:00:06,254
Their query boxes look alike.

3
00:00:06,417 --> 00:00:08,188
Are you licensing the same retrieval

4
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:11,435
design? Pause and ask what each accepts:

5
00:00:11,713 --> 00:00:15,391
only text, or fields, a seed paper,

6
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:18,253
citation links, saved judgements and API

7
00:00:18,273 --> 00:00:19,218
predicates?

8
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:24,136
For an agentic mode, ask whether both the

9
00:00:24,156 --> 00:00:26,623
task brief and its generated queries can

10
00:00:26,643 --> 00:00:29,188
be exported. A convenient text box can

11
00:00:29,208 --> 00:00:31,507
narrow the starting method before ranking

12
00:00:31,527 --> 00:00:34,716
begins. The chapter turns documentation

13
00:00:34,736 --> 00:00:36,842
and inspection into nineteen vendor

14
00:00:36,862 --> 00:00:39,677
questions, grouped into six areas.

15
00:00:39,852 --> 00:00:42,474
They are questions to verify, not answers

16
00:00:42,494 --> 00:00:43,968
supplied by this film.

17
00:00:44,903 --> 00:00:47,383
First, what does the system infer, change

18
00:00:47,403 --> 00:00:50,630
and decide? Separate recognising fields or

19
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:53,968
intent, transforming inputs, selecting

20
00:00:53,988 --> 00:00:56,519
routes and constructing another query from

21
00:00:56,539 --> 00:00:57,691
earlier results.

22
00:00:57,841 --> 00:01:00,140
Ask to inspect and export each

23
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:03,271
transformation, route and feedback record.

24
00:01:03,824 --> 00:01:06,482
Second, who controls the trajectory?

25
00:01:06,631 --> 00:01:09,279
Is the sequence prescribed, selected among

26
00:01:09,299 --> 00:01:12,487
designer enumerated branches, or planned

27
00:01:12,507 --> 00:01:13,763
from observations?

28
00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:17,384
A rule, classifier or model may choose an

29
00:01:17,404 --> 00:01:18,660
adaptive branch.

30
00:01:18,861 --> 00:01:21,122
For model planned actions, ask which

31
00:01:21,142 --> 00:01:24,008
tools, sources and iteration limits bound

32
00:01:24,028 --> 00:01:26,689
the sequence and whether every action and

33
00:01:26,709 --> 00:01:28,221
stop is visible.

34
00:01:29,126 --> 00:01:31,594
Ask which retrieval and ranking components

35
00:01:31,614 --> 00:01:34,764
run, whether in parallel or sequence, and

36
00:01:34,784 --> 00:01:36,580
how many candidates survive.

37
00:01:36,756 --> 00:01:39,660
Ask what job the neural model performs:

38
00:01:39,861 --> 00:01:42,032
query interpretation, first stage

39
00:01:42,052 --> 00:01:44,867
representation, sparse expansion, joint

40
00:01:44,887 --> 00:01:47,495
reranking or final answer generation.

41
00:01:47,632 --> 00:01:49,906
A model name alone does not describe the

42
00:01:49,926 --> 00:01:50,975
architecture.

43
00:01:51,525 --> 00:01:53,722
Ask the indexed unit and whether later

44
00:01:53,742 --> 00:01:56,234
full text fetching is separate.

45
00:01:56,384 --> 00:01:59,650
An abstract index cannot match full text

46
00:01:59,670 --> 00:02:01,608
only evidence at that stage.

47
00:02:01,771 --> 00:02:04,096
Ask how multiple passage matches from one

48
00:02:04,116 --> 00:02:05,655
paper are assembled.

49
00:02:05,869 --> 00:02:08,606
Finally, ask where hybrid component lists

50
00:02:08,626 --> 00:02:12,073
are fused, which cutoffs and rerankers

51
00:02:12,093 --> 00:02:13,941
follow, and whether component

52
00:02:13,961 --> 00:02:15,913
contributions can be inspected or

53
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:16,776
controlled.

54
00:02:17,685 --> 00:02:20,398
Ask whether an exact lexical route

55
00:02:20,418 --> 00:02:22,950
survives for identifiers and quoted

56
00:02:22,970 --> 00:02:26,557
phrases. Ask how case, punctuation,

57
00:02:26,694 --> 00:02:29,625
hyphens and identifiers are analysed, and

58
00:02:29,645 --> 00:02:32,176
whether query and document analysis agree.

59
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:34,934
For dense inputs, ask which token

60
00:02:34,954 --> 00:02:38,091
representation is used and how unfamiliar

61
00:02:38,111 --> 00:02:39,392
strings are tested.

62
00:02:39,948 --> 00:02:43,548
Ask for exactness, negation, exclusions,

63
00:02:43,568 --> 00:02:46,151
contradictory claims and near duplicate

64
00:02:46,171 --> 00:02:48,600
name tests. Then ask what trained the

65
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:50,907
relevance model and how it was adapted to

66
00:02:50,927 --> 00:02:53,380
local disciplines and document types.

67
00:02:53,543 --> 00:02:56,242
Web questions, citation links and

68
00:02:56,262 --> 00:02:58,381
scholarly judgements reward different

69
00:02:58,401 --> 00:03:01,409
relationships. A paraphrase demonstration

70
00:03:01,429 --> 00:03:03,496
does not answer these questions.

71
00:03:04,404 --> 00:03:06,364
Ask whether users can trace a result

72
00:03:06,384 --> 00:03:08,490
backwards through actual inputs,

73
00:03:08,510 --> 00:03:11,582
constraints, candidate routes, evidence,

74
00:03:11,745 --> 00:03:13,348
ranking and display.

75
00:03:13,510 --> 00:03:15,861
Require a distinction between execution

76
00:03:15,881 --> 00:03:18,528
evidence and a post hoc explanation.

77
00:03:18,704 --> 00:03:21,171
Ask whether the exact generated inputs,

78
00:03:21,191 --> 00:03:24,792
routes, mode, versions, index date,

79
00:03:24,812 --> 00:03:27,575
cutoffs and identifiers can be exported.

80
00:03:28,127 --> 00:03:31,030
On rerun, does the product reuse a saved

81
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:33,465
transformation or generate it again?

82
00:03:33,627 --> 00:03:36,365
Ask whether model, index and ranking

83
00:03:36,385 --> 00:03:38,723
changes are disclosed, including which

84
00:03:38,743 --> 00:03:40,656
version produced a saved run.

85
00:03:40,831 --> 00:03:42,576
These are requirements for later

86
00:03:42,596 --> 00:03:45,025
comparison, not a promise of identical

87
00:03:45,045 --> 00:03:46,339
results forever.

88
00:03:47,223 --> 00:03:51,086
Ask what a search costs: seats, queries or

89
00:03:51,106 --> 00:03:53,767
tokens, with which rate and iteration

90
00:03:53,787 --> 00:03:57,361
limits. What happens at a limit: refusal,

91
00:03:57,511 --> 00:04:00,570
truncation or a silently shallower search?

92
00:04:00,745 --> 00:04:04,230
Does agentic mode cost differently, and

93
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:06,099
can the library inspect per query

94
00:04:06,119 --> 00:04:07,000
consumption?

95
00:04:07,571 --> 00:04:10,013
Ask what happens when a mode is retired.

96
00:04:10,175 --> 00:04:13,377
Can saved searches, result sets and traces

97
00:04:13,397 --> 00:04:16,224
be exported, and how much notice is given?

98
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:18,454
The chapter cites renamed and distinct

99
00:04:18,474 --> 00:04:20,992
product modes as reasons to ask.

100
00:04:21,142 --> 00:04:23,222
It does not claim a new retirement event.

101
00:04:23,371 --> 00:04:26,289
Continuity depends on exportable records

102
00:04:26,309 --> 00:04:28,518
and explicit change arrangements.

103
00:04:29,431 --> 00:04:32,101
Ask how performance is evaluated, and on

104
00:04:32,121 --> 00:04:35,130
whose queries. Include the institution’s

105
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:38,416
disciplines, vocabulary, languages,

106
00:04:38,436 --> 00:04:41,250
document types and known relevant records.

107
00:04:41,425 --> 00:04:44,176
Ask whether known failure cases belong in

108
00:04:44,196 --> 00:04:46,908
evaluation, rather than relying only on

109
00:04:46,928 --> 00:04:49,510
the product’s strongest demonstrations.

110
00:04:50,058 --> 00:04:52,731
Finally, can the library rerun local test

111
00:04:52,751 --> 00:04:55,914
queries across a model, index or ranking

112
00:04:55,934 --> 00:04:59,394
update? Save the baseline and inspect per

113
00:04:59,414 --> 00:05:02,267
query differences, so a regression omitted

114
00:05:02,287 --> 00:05:04,792
from release notes can become visible.

115
00:05:04,968 --> 00:05:07,177
These questions connect procurement to the

116
00:05:07,197 --> 00:05:10,373
local comparisons of Chapter fourteen; no

117
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,872
vendor benchmark is being performed here.

118
00:05:13,765 --> 00:05:16,305
Documentation and inspection cannot be

119
00:05:16,325 --> 00:05:18,896
relied on to arrive on a library’s

120
00:05:18,916 --> 00:05:20,957
timetable after licensing.

121
00:05:21,132 --> 00:05:23,432
Ask for evidence, record the vendor’s

122
00:05:23,452 --> 00:05:26,717
response, verify what the library can test

123
00:05:26,944 --> 00:05:28,934
and keep follow up for unknowns.

124
00:05:29,096 --> 00:05:31,099
The accompanying question sheet leaves

125
00:05:31,119 --> 00:05:32,993
those answers blank.

126
00:05:33,549 --> 00:05:35,697
Libraries need enough visibility to

127
00:05:35,717 --> 00:05:37,849
